# Vercel builds the frontend and nothing else. The backend is on Render.
#
# Belt and braces beside vercel.json's "framework": null. Vercel inspects the
# repository to guess what it is holding, and a requirements.txt next to a
# manage.py makes it guess Django. It then imports the settings module, which
# fails on the first line that reads a secret - so the error names SECRET_KEY
# and reads like a missing environment variable, when what actually happened
# is that the wrong project was built.
backend/
requirements.txt
build.sh
DEPLOY.md
render.yaml

# Never uploaded anywhere, but especially not here.
venv/
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
*.log
